entries=[('O016','one-page-marketing-plan-example','''<section id="day6-ai-effort"><h2>Keep AI production effort separate from campaign contribution</h2><p>Fast drafting does not remove review time. For a fictional four-asset plan, 30 drafting minutes and 20 review minutes per asset total 200 minutes. Two extra revisions at 20 minutes each add 40, making 240 minutes against 180 available: a 60-minute capacity gap. This is a production workload example, separate from the existing $600 campaign contribution test.</p><p>Use the <a href="/journal/ai-marketing-workflow-examples/">AI marketing workflow examples</a> to define approved facts, review and rework, and the <a href="/tools/strategic-plan-template/">strategic-plan worksheet</a> to assign the action owner, metric and resources. Include labor in a financial comparison only under a declared cost boundary; do not subtract a cost again if it is already in the campaign budget. A completed content task is not proof of a retained order.</p></section>'''),('O018','one-page-business-plan-template-assumptions','''<section id="day6-action-versus-outcome"><h2>Keep action completion separate from the outcome test</h2><p>Completing a pilot checklist does not establish that its target was achieved. In an original fictional example, a baseline of 20 qualified inquiries, target 40 and current 30 represent 50% of the intended baseline-to-target change. One completed action out of three is 33.3% action completion. Keep the measurement definition, source and comparable periods beside those separate figures.</p><p>The <a href="/tools/strategic-plan-template/">one-objective strategic-plan worksheet</a> links a measurable outcome to action owners, deadlines, allocated cost and available minutes. It is a working action sheet rather than a replacement for this business-plan assumptions log. Compare 480 planned minutes with 420 available to expose a 60-minute gap, even if a $350 budget exceeds $300 of allocations. The budget surplus does not resolve the time constraint.</p></section>''')]
